From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH v2] serial: qcom-geni: power off every open port across system suspend

qcom_geni_serial_suspend() switches the console port's interconnect votes to
QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY "so we can hit the lowest possible state in
suspend".  Every other port that is open across suspend has a worse
version of the problem: uart_suspend_port() shuts it down and drops its
UART_PM_STATE, but that is only a runtime PM put, which cannot suspend the
device while the PM core holds it from prepare to complete.  The port stays
powered: its ALWAYS-tagged votes stay in the RPMh sleep set and its SE
clock stays prepared, which keeps the GCC PLL (gpll0) and the RPMh XO
voted on through suspend.

On the Retroid Pocket 5 the gamepad MCU (serdev on 888000.serial) and the
QCA6390 Bluetooth (serdev on 998000.serial) are open all the time.  With
the clk core transitions traced through a suspend, gcc_qupv3_wrap0_s6_clk
and gcc_qupv3_wrap2_s2_clk were the last prepared clocks under bi_tcxo at
the RPMh flush, and their votes kept QUP0/CN0/SN11 in the sleep set.

Apply the console's tag switch to every port, and force the runtime
suspend (and resume) of non-console ports that are not wakeup sources
around uart_suspend_port()/uart_resume_port().  v1 did only the tag switch.
---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c	2026-10-16 13:25:03.218283676 +0900
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c	2026-10-16 14:14:34.099902685 +0900
@@ -1975,15 +1975,31 @@
 	struct uart_port *uport = &port->uport;
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
 
+	int ret;
+
 	/*
 	 * This is done so we can hit the lowest possible state in suspend
-	 * even with no_console_suspend
+	 * even with no_console_suspend, and for every other port.
 	 */
-	if (uart_console(uport)) {
-		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY);
-		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
-	}
-	return uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY);
+	geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
+
+	ret = uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * uart_suspend_port() shuts a non-console port down and asks for it to
+	 * be powered off, but that is a runtime PM put, which cannot suspend
+	 * the device while the PM core holds it from prepare to complete. An
+	 * open port (a serdev client such as Bluetooth or a gamepad MCU) then
+	 * keeps its SE clock prepared through suspend, and with it the GCC
+	 * PLL and the RPMh XO in the sleep set. Force the runtime suspend.
+	 */
+	if (!uart_console(uport) && !device_may_wakeup(dev))
+		return pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int qcom_geni_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
@@ -1993,11 +2009,15 @@
 	struct uart_port *uport = &port->uport;
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
 
-	ret = uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
-	if (uart_console(uport)) {
-		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS);
-		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
+	if (!uart_console(uport) && !device_may_wakeup(dev)) {
+		ret = pm_runtime_force_resume(dev);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
 	}
+
+	ret = uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS);
+	geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
 	return ret;
 }
 
